<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Oct trade surplus 3.9 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.African Oct trade surplus 3.9 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa recorded a trade surplus of 3.9 billion rand in October from a 666.7 million rand surplus in September, according to latest South African Revenue Service figures.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast an average 900 million rand surplus.  </p>
<p>(Data in billions of rand - rounded)</p>
<p>			Oct '96	     Sept '96	   Oct '95</p>
<p>Exports	     14.90		 10.96		 8.01</p>
<p>Imports	     11.00		 10.29		 9.08</p>
<p>Balance		3.90		  0.67		-1.07</p>
<p>			Jan-Oct '96	 Jan-Oct '95</p>
<p>Exports	     104.20		84.85</p>
<p>Imports		96.04		82.70</p>
<p>Balance		 8.16		 2.15</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom (+27 11 482-1003)</p>
</text>
